WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.816
Let’s open ChatGPT and try a short conversation.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.307
You’ll send a message, read the reply, and ask for one
change.

00:00:10.398 --> 00:00:15.135
In the Academy guide, select Open ChatGPT in a new tab.

00:00:16.094 --> 00:00:17.797
Keep the Academy tab open.

00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:21.702
You don’t need to download a computer app for this
exercise.

00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:28.509
If you already have an account, choose Log in and use
the same method you used before.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.849
If this is your first time, choose Sign up and follow
the instructions on your screen.

00:00:35.838 --> 00:00:38.194
A free account is enough for this exercise.

00:00:39.137 --> 00:00:46.143
If you are asked for a verification code, find the
email from OpenAI and enter the code on the sign-in
screen.

00:00:47.063 --> 00:00:50.828
Keep passwords and verification codes out of chat
messages.

00:00:51.907 --> 00:00:54.065
Once you see the message box, you’re ready.

00:00:55.044 --> 00:00:58.719
A prompt is the question or instruction you give AI.

00:00:59.645 --> 00:01:02.356
Select the message box and enter this request:

00:01:03.405 --> 00:01:06.548
Suggest three simple activities for a family gathering.

00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:10.766
You can type it yourself or copy it from the Academy
guide.

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:15.448
Select the send arrow on the right, then wait for the
reply.

00:01:16.477 --> 00:01:17.635
Read the suggestions.

00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:25.748
In this example, ChatGPT suggested family trivia,
sharing photos and stories, and a team game.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.146
Your reply may be different.

00:01:29.042 --> 00:01:32.285
Think about who will be there and which activity would
suit them.

00:01:33.278 --> 00:01:35.334
Pause here if you would like time to read.

00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:37.888
Keep this conversation open.

00:01:38.595 --> 00:01:41.027
In the message box below the reply, write:

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.142
Make them suitable for indoors, without buying
supplies.

00:01:46.241 --> 00:01:46.914
Then send it.

00:01:47.823 --> 00:01:49.453
You can add details as you go.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.340
You don’t have to start a new conversation.

00:01:53.532 --> 00:01:55.093
Now read the new suggestions.

00:01:55.979 --> 00:01:57.235
Would they work indoors?

00:01:57.999 --> 00:01:59.733
Do they use things you already have?

00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:04.901
If something doesn’t fit, tell ChatGPT what needs
changing.

00:02:05.856 --> 00:02:07.995
You decide which suggestions to use.

00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:11.151
Pause whenever you want to try a step yourself.

00:02:12.077 --> 00:02:14.769
Select the Academy tab at the top of your browser.

00:02:15.751 --> 00:02:19.618
Leave ChatGPT open so you can switch back during
practice.

00:02:20.574 --> 00:02:25.043
You’ve opened ChatGPT, sent a message, and asked for a
change.

00:02:26.034 --> 00:02:29.201
Use the checklist in the guide to see which steps
you’ve tried.

00:02:30.134 --> 00:02:34.749
You can repeat any step, or continue to Lesson one
point one when you’re ready.
